  "narrative": "Direction convention: all outcome_006 claims in this run use hypothesis direction -1, so a positive signed estimate means stronger dependency, i.e. a more negative raw outcome_006 score in feature_060=1 than in feature_060=0. The absolute outcome_006 mean is about 0.175, so the 10% clinical threshold is approximately 0.0175 score units.\n\nI accept H146 as a supported but imprecise dataset-specific direct effect-modification contrast. H146 asks whether the feature_060 contrast is stronger in the high feature_024 quartile than in its complement. The discovery interaction was +0.0583, about 33.2% of the absolute outcome_006 mean, and the independent validation was +0.0277, about 15.8% of the absolute mean. Both point estimates are above the clinical threshold and in the same favorable direction. The validation interval is wide and includes zero and values below the threshold, so the precision is low. I do not treat H146 as causal, generalizable, or as proof that feature_024 has a simple monotone modifier; rather, it supports the dataset-specific possibility that the accepted H142 association is larger in the feature_024 upper quartile.\n\nThe central accepted finding remains H142: among observations with feature_024 at or above its median, feature_060=1 is associated with stronger outcome_006 dependency than feature_060=0, with discovery and independent validation estimates both well above the clinical threshold. The new H146 evidence refines this by suggesting that the feature_024-high signal may be especially apparent in the top quartile, but the effect-modification claim is uncertain because of the wide validation interval and because thresholds were explored.\n\nGradient evidence is mixed but consistent with upper-tail concentration. H147, the low-quartile negative control, is near null and rejected. H148, the median-to-Q3 band, is below threshold and imprecise. H150/H151, the extreme tail, have large point estimates but small cells and very wide intervals, so they remain closed unresolved rather than accepted. H145, the high-quartile simple effect, remains unresolved but important because its point estimate is large; I do not accept it alone because it lacks independent validation and arises from threshold exploration.\n\nFeature_034 is the key next modifier. Within feature_024 at or above the median, the feature_060 contrast is strong when feature_034=1, H152 estimate +0.0673 with a discovery interval barely excluding zero, and near null when feature_034=0, H153 estimate +0.0111. H152 is compelling but nested and selected, so I do not yet accept it. The corrected interaction H159 has not been analyzed, and I registered high-quartile extensions to test whether the accepted H146 interaction is concentrated with feature_034.\n\nOutcome specificity is supported. In the same feature_024-high subgroup, outcome_008, outcome_011, and outcome_013 are null, opposite, or below threshold, and outcome_008 interaction is null/opposite. This argues against a broad dependency effect across outcomes and strengthens outcome_006 specificity. Earlier validation assessments for H104, H88, and H114 remain rejected: their independent evidence was inconsistent or too weak relative to threshold.\n\nNegative findings across many nominal categorical and high-prevalence binary marker families remain closed, reducing support for other predictor associations. The most informative next analysis is to test the feature_034 overlap: analyze H159 and the new high-quartile feature_034 proposals, and if budget permits, independently validate H152 or H159. If H152/H159 validates positively, I would consider a narrower dataset-specific intersection claim involving feature_024 high and feature_034=1. If validation is null, I would retain H142 and H146 as broader feature_024-associated contrasts, while downgrading feature_034-specific concentration.",
  "research_notes": "Accepted dataset-specific findings: H142, outcome_006 feature_060=1 vs 0 within feature_024 >= median; H146, high feature_024 quartile direct interaction, positive discovery +0.0583 and validation +0.0277, but imprecise and low confidence in magnitude. All outcome_006 claims direction -1; positive signed = stronger dependency. 10% threshold about 0.0175.\n\nCurrent priority: determine whether feature_034 explains or concentrates the feature_024-high signal. Keep H152 active as the strongest nested simple effect, discovery +0.0673 with CI barely excluding zero, but unvalidated and selected. H153 is near null. H159 corrected median high feature_034 interaction is active and untested. New proposals: high quartile feature_034 simple effect and high quartile feature_034 interaction.\n\nGradient controls: H145 active, high quartile simple effect +0.0631, no validation; H147 low quartile rejected; H148 middle band below threshold closed unresolved; H150/H151 extreme tail closed unresolved due small cells. Do not reopen these unless a better design is available.\n\nOutcome specificity: H155/H156/H157/H158 reject outcome_008, outcome_011, outcome_013 extension; supports narrow outcome_006 association.\n\nValidation budget: 5 remaining. Next validation target if allowed: H152 first, then H159 or H144. If H152 validates null, retain H142/H146 but close feature_034 concentration. If positive, accept a refined feature_024-high and feature_034=1 intersection claim with careful uncertainty language. Do not interpret accepted claims as causal or generalizable."
}

